<speak>Yes, the separation is important to me. At the office, everyone is used to passing a folder around, but my personal banking is not part of that system. I keep those papers myself. My nephew is helpful with the business calendar, and my wife helps me remember family arrangements, but neither of them needs to sit in on every conversation I have. Recently I realised I was spending too much time reacting to whatever arrived first. I would like a more orderly routine, even if the business schedule itself remains messy. At least the personal paperwork should not become another source of confusion.</speak>